cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use GIK-IceChain in your research or operations, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "GIK-IceChain v2.0: Zero-Cost Cloud-Native Pipeline for Retrospective Flood Risk Decision Support in East Africa"
abstract: >
  GIK-IceChain v2.0 transforms the ECMWF IFS ensemble archive (>1 PB of GRIB2 data)
  into an operational flood risk decision-support system for East Africa, at near-zero
  storage cost, using IceChunk Zarr v3 virtual stores, adaptive GEV exceedance thresholds,
  and the ICPAC CRMA Bayesian Network with Dynamic BN extensions.
version: "2.0.0"
date-released: "2026-08-31"
license: Apache-2.0
url: "https://github.com/hashirama21/gik-icechain"
repository-code: "https://github.com/hashirama21/gik-icechain"

keywords:
  - ECMWF
  - IFS ensemble
  - flood risk
  - East Africa
  - cloud-native
  - Zarr
  - IceChunk
  - VirtualiZarr
  - GRIB2
  - Bayesian network
  - CRMA
  - ICPAC
  - anticipatory action

